cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FORGE in academic or industry research, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "FORGE — Synthetic Policy Book + Multi-Peril Scenario Set"
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >
  FORGE is a scenario-coupled catastrophe-operations console for primary
  insurers and reinsurers. A single Monte-Carlo scenario set drives three
  optimization layers simultaneously — Portfolio MIP (CBC + PuLP), Operational
  LP (VRP for adjuster routing), and a claims pre-flagger — through a shared
  Decision Reconciler. The deposit bundles the synthetic 10,000-policy book,
  the multi-peril scenario set (hurricane, severe-convective-storm, wildfire,
  earthquake, winter storm), and the full codebase that generates and
  consumes them.
authors:
  - family-names: Devaraju
    given-names: Sagar
    affiliation: FORGE
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sagardevaraju/forge"
url: "https://github.com/sagardevaraju/forge"
keywords:
  - reinsurance
  - catastrophe modeling
  - portfolio optimization
  - synthetic data
  - HAZUS
  - HURDAT2
  - Monte Carlo
  - stochastic optimization
  - insurance
  - natural hazards
